calation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"apps/web/src/lib/api-client.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Frontend API client must never expose 'db' (unscoped) operations. All data fetches must go through 'db.<model>.<operation>' which enforces ZenStack policies. Verify no direct fetch() calls bypass this.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"apps/api/src/server/storage.ts (S3 setup)\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"S3 presigned URLs (presigned POST/GET) are time-limited, but verify: (1) presigned URLs expire quickly, (2) upload ACLs prevent cross-org access, (3) file listings require auth.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"apps/api/src/routes/conversations.ts\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Typing indicators and read receipts expose user presence. Verify these are only sent to authorized group/conversation members to prevent user enumeration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"apps/web/src/components/chat/\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rich text rendering (RichText component) could render unsanitized HTML if user content isn't escaped. Verify dangerouslySetInnerHTML is never used; use React's JSX (auto-escapes) or a sanitizer like DOMPurify.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \".env.example\",\n      \"line\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Environment variables for S3, TURN, and Resend API keys are required at runtime. Ensure these are never committed to .env (should stay in .env.example only). CI/CD must inject them securely.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 62,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"**Audit ZenStack policies**: Run `bun --cwd apps/api run test` and verify `tests/policies.test.ts` covers all multi-tenant entities. Check that every top-level model (Group, Conversation, Event, Call, Attachment, Notification) has `@@deny('all', !(organization.members?[...]))`. Missing guards = data leaks.\",\n    \"**Verify db vs. userDb usage**: Grep the codebase for `const db =` and `userDb =` in route handlers. Every user-driven operation must use `userDb = dbFor(user)`. Any `db` used for user input bypasses policies.\",\n    \"**Validate WebSocket handlers**: In `src/websocket/hub.ts`, `index.ts`, and `calls.ts`, check that socket event handlers validate incoming payloads against Zod/Elysia schemas. Test with malformed/oversized messages.\",\n    \"**Rate-limit verification**: Test `/api/execute` rate limit (300/min) by sending a batch with 100 operations in one request. Confirm the server rejects or queues it, not allows 100 ops in one call.\",\n    \"**Admin field protection test**: Add a test in `tests/user-admin-fields.test.ts` that attempts to update `role`, `banned`, and `permissions` fields as a regular user. Should fail with 403 or not-found.\",\n    \"**Sanitize rich text**: If RichText components render user posts/comments, audit `src/components/chat/` and `feed/` to ensure no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Use DOMPurify if HTML is needed.\",\n    \"**S3 access control**: Verify S3 bucket policy: (1) presigned URLs are read-only or write-only scoped, (2) cross-tenant uploads are blocked (test uploading to another org's files), (3) list-objects is denied for anonymous/cross-org users.\",\n    \"**Secrets management**: Ensure `.env` is in `.gitignore` and never committed. Use separate `.env.local` for development. In CI/CD, inject secrets via environment variables or secret management (AWS Secrets Manager, etc.).\",\n    \"**Dependency scanning**: Run `npm audit` (or `bun install --production` then audit) monthly. Pin versions in package.json and use Dependabot or Snyk for automated checks.\",\n    \"**CSRF protection**: Verify POST/PUT/DELETE routes use the SameSite cookie flag (better-auth should do this). Test with a cross-origin form POST to confirm rejection.\",\n    \"**Input validation**: All route handlers should validate body/query with Elysia `t` schemas. Fuzz test with SQLi payloads (`'; DROP TABLE --`), XXS payloads (`<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>`), and oversized arrays.\",\n    \"**Audit tenant-switching logic**: In `src/server/org.ts` and auth hooks, verify org membership changes (add/remove members) immediately update active groups and conversation memberships. Test removing a user and confirming they can't read old messages.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Risk Score: 62/100** — Medium-High Risk\n\n### Most Critical Issues\n\n1. **Tenant Isolation (High)**: The codebase's core security depends on ZenStack policies enforcing `@@deny` rules. Any missing guard or incorrect `auth()` check in the schema breaks data isolation across organizations. The tests must be comprehensive.\n\n2. **Policy Enforcement Path (High)**: All user-driven queries must use `dbFor(user)` (yielding `userDb`). Accidentally using the unscoped `db` client in a route handler would bypass all policies. This requires code review discipline.\n\n3. **WebSocket Validation (Medium)**: Real-time events and WebRTC signaling rely on socket handlers; unvalidated payloads could corrupt state or trigger unauthorized actions.\n\n### Secondary Issues\n\n- Rate-limit bypass risk if `/api/execute` counts batch size as 1 request instead of N operations.\n- S3 presigned URL scope and expiry need verification to prevent cross-tenant file access.\n- Rich text rendering could XSS if user content isn't escaped (React JSX auto-escapes, but verify no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`).\n\n### What's Done Right\n\n✅ Tenant isolation design is sound (ZenStack policies + per-user auth context)  \n✅ Admin-only fields marked with `@deny('update', true)`  \n✅ Rate-limiting in place  \n✅ React auto-escapes text content (XSS resistant)  \n✅ Authentication via better-auth (standard, secure library)\n\n---\n\n**Next Step**: Run `bun --cwd apps/api run test` to verify policy tests, then conduct a code review of `routes/` and `websocket/` handlers for validation gaps.\n",
